    "abstract": "The effects of climate change on the Tibetan Plateau are most serious and the most sensitive. Changes in vegetation are some of the most important signs of ecological change. This paper examines the consequences of global warming on vegetation in the plateau. Using MODIS remote sensing data and the CN05.1 meteorological dataset, vegetation and climate change trends have been compared and analyzed. The climate of the Qinghai-Tibet plateau as a whole is becoming warmer, and wetter. In particular, the northwest is changing from warm and dry to warm and wet. Vegetation growth plateau as a whole is improving, especially in the grassland region, but regional differences do exist.",
    "field": "Impact of climate change on vegetation",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of determining the consequences of global warming on vegetation in the Tibetan Plateau, where high ecological sensitivity and regional climate variations create complex spatio-temporal changes that are critical to monitor and understand.",
    "method": "This paper compares MODIS remote sensing vegetation data and CN05.1 meteorological data from 2001-2022, creating spatial distribution maps and using variance analysis to examine the trends and consequences of global warming on vegetation in the Tibetan Plateau.",
    "task": "The task is to examine the impact of global warming on vegetation in the Tibetan Plateau by analyzing and comparing MODIS remote sensing data with CN05.1 meteorological data from 2001 to 2022.",
